    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d280-a2">

                <pb facs="0394" n="288" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg288"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Miss Ericksen to Mr.
                            Martin.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-08-15"><hi rendition="#small-caps">August</hi> 15,
                            1906</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Martin</hi>: I am writing these few lines to
                    ask a favor of you. We have under our care a Chinese baby girl who was thrown
                    out to die by her parents and we want to know if it is possible to take her with
                    us to the United States next spring. If so, under what conditions. I wish to
                    adopt her and have her brought up in my home as an American citizen. Will you
                    let me hear from you at your earliest convenience, and oblige,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Carrie M.
                    Ericksen.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
